@startuml

!include fta_metamodel.puml

$FailureMode("shm-object created with wrong permissions", "Memory.CreateAppliesWrongPermissions")
' Guideword -> Corruption
' FailureEffect: Another process can access the data within shm and corrupt it!

$OrGate("Gate1", "Memory.CreateAppliesWrongPermissions")

' -> this can only happen, when the creator crashes between creating and applying permissions
' but since we have our Lockfile still exist, no one can access -> No issue -> NO FTA!
' we can also not follow, that maybe a user called RemoveStaleArtefacts() because it would have removed the shm-object as well.

$IntermediateEvent("Permissions have not been applied correctly", "Memory.CrashedBeforeApplyPerm", "Gate1")
$RootCause("shm-object already exists with wrong permissions", "Memory.ShmObjectAlreadyExists", "Gate1")

$OrGate("Gate2", "Memory.CrashedBeforeApplyPerm")

$RootCause("Creating process crashed before applying permissions", "Memory.ProcessCrashedBetweenCreationAndPermissions", "Gate2")
$RootCause("Creator did not apply correct permissions", "Memory.CreatorDidNotSetPermissions", "Gate2")

@enduml




@enduml